\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Vietnam to pay attention to monetary policy after U.S. report - c.bank official\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2021\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Corrects to delete extraneous word "the" in the first paragraph, add missing word "bank" in paragraph 6.)\par \par \uc2 HANOI, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Vietnam will pay more attention to its monetary policy as it is not only a domestic matter but a concern for the country's big trade partners, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor said on Sunday, days after the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's semi-annual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/us-treasury-says-vietnam-taiwan-exceed-currency-thresholds-no-manipulator-labels-2021-12-03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/us-treasury-says-vietnam-taiwan-exceed-\b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22 -thresholds-no-manipulator-labels-2021-12-03}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  report on Friday said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeded its trade surplus, current account and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  thresholds, but was "satisfied with progress made by \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  to date" on addressing exchange-rate issues.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an economic forum, Pham Thanh Ha, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said the bank had taken the issues seriously and its monetary policy towards them had been implemented effectively.\par \par \uc2 "We have to pay more attention to our monetary policy implementation as it does not have impact on our domestic economy but our big trade partners as well," Ha said.\par \par \uc2 "Vietnam will keep implementing monetary policy in a cautious and flexible manner."\par \par \uc2 Ha also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $25 billion worth of dollars over the past two years to help inject dong into the banking system and boost the economy.\par \par \uc2 If necessary, he said, the bank would have to implement measures that would affect liquidity and market interest rates amid rising inflation risks. (Editing by Alex Richardson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-12-6T03:38:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211205ehc500j25\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
