\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Vietnam pledges not to devalue  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  in agreement with \uc2 U.S. Treasury\b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2021\par 20:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds statement from USTR, details on Vietnam's U.S. trade surplus)\par \par \uc2 By David Lawder and Lisa Lambert\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, July 19 (Reuters) - Vietnam has pledged not to deliberately weaken its dong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain an export advantage, reaching an agreement with the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  to refrain from "competitive devaluation" and make its monetary and exchange rate policies more transparent.\par \par \uc2 The agreement, announced in a joint statement by Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  Governor \uc2 Nguyen Thi Hong\uc2  after a virtual meeting on Monday, follows months of U.S. pressure on Vietnam over its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices and ballooning U.S. trade surplus.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration in its final weeks had declared Vietnam a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator and had threatened to impose punitive tariffs on imports from Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam, which benefited from the shift of U.S. supply chains away from China amid a tariff war, saw its goods trade surplus with the United State jump 25% in 2020 to $69.7 billion despite the COVID-19 pandemic. Vietnam is a growing source of U.S. imports of furniture, electronics, computers and apparel.\par \par \uc2 In the joint statement, Vietnam confirmed its commitment under \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  rules "to avoid manipulating its exchange rate in order to prevent effective balance of payments adjustment or to gain an unfair competitive advantage and will refrain from any competitive devaluation of the Vietnamese dong."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Vietnamese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the focus of its monetary policy framework is "to promote macroeconomic stability and to control inflation."\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to "improve exchange rate flexibility over time," allowing the dong to move in line with the development of the country's markets and economic fundamentals, and to further modernize and make more transparent its monetary policy and exchange rate framework\par \par \uc2 The Treasury said it would inform other \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  agencies about the agreement to address U.S. concerns.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attention to these issues over time not only will address Treasury\u8217\'20\'19s concerns, but also will support the further development of Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s financial markets and enhance its macroeconomic and financial resilience," Yellen said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury under Yellen in April removed a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator" label from Vietnam that had been imposed by the Trump administration last December. But the Treasury said that Vietnam, along with Taiwan and Switzerland, had tripped its thresholds for the designation under a 2015 law.\par \par \uc2 The department at the time said it would commence "enhanced engagement" with Hanoi to correct the situation, which led \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global current account surplus to exceed 2% of its GDP.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Trade Representative Katherine Tai said her agency will monitor Hanoi's implementation of the agreement and would work with Vietnam "to ensure that it addresses the acts, policies and practices related to the valuation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were found actionable in the Section 301 investigation."\par \par \uc2 USTR's probe had found that Vietnam was taking "unreasonable" actions to push down the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make its exports cheaper, but held off on imposing tariffs. (Reporting by Lisa Lambert; Editing by Angus MacSwan and Andrea Ricci) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-7-19T19:00:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210719eh7j02plx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
