\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 , \uc2 Vietnam  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Reach Agreement on  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Practices -- 2nd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kate Davidson \par \uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2021\par 16:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has agreed to improve the flexibility of its exchange rate as part of a continued effort to make its monetary policy and exchange rate framework more transparent, following a meeting between Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and Vietnam State Bank \uc2 Gov. Nguyen Thi Hong\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration last year labeled Vietnam a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator and threatened to impose sweeping tariffs on imports from Vietnam. The Biden administration reversed the "manipulator" designation in April, saying it found insufficient evidence that the country was manipulating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but hasn't yet completed the process that could lead to the imposition of tariffs.\par \par \uc2 U.S. policy makers and the business community have increased their focus on Vietnam as the country has risen, in just the past decade, from a minor trading partner to the No. 6 source of U.S. imports, trailing only China, Mexico, Canada, Japan and Germany.\par \par \uc2 In a joint statement Monday, Ms. Yellen and Ms. Nguyen said the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  reiterated that the focus of its monetary policy framework is to promote macroeconomic stability and control inflation.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has agreed to allow the Vietnamese dong to move "in line with the state of development of the financial and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and with economic fundamentals," according to the statement. Vietnam pledged not to lower its exchange rate to give its exporters a competitive advantage.\par \par \uc2 It will also continue to provide necessary information for the Treasury to conduct thorough analysis and reporting on its activities in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as part of Treasury's regular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report to Congress.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2 's attention to these issues over time not only will address Treasury's concerns, but also will support the further development of Vietnam's financial markets and enhance its macroeconomic and financial resilience," Ms. Yellen said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 The Trump Treasury Department in December said \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in a persistent, one-sided manner to limit appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and had also sought to gain unfair competitive advantage in international trade through its exchange-rate management.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration removed that label in April, but said it would continue discussions with Vietnamese officials on their economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 In their statement Monday, Ms. Yellen and Ms. Hong said the U.S. and Vietnam are "trusted partners with friendship grounded in mutual respect, " and said they are committed to maintaining close cooperation between their two institutions.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hong said \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to manage its exchange rate "to safeguard the proper functioning of the monetary and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, to promote macroeconomic stability and to control inflation, not to create an unfair competitive advantage in international trade."\par \par \uc2 --Josh Zumbrun contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kate Davidson at kate.davidson@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 19, 2021 10:11 ET (14:11 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020210719eh7j0035w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
