\par\par \b \uc2 More Asian countries thick-skinned about  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  manipulator tag\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2021\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HANOI/SHANGHAI, April 13 (Reuters) - A larger number of Asian countries and economies could join the ranks of those branded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  in the coming days, and yet that prospect is barely causing any concern in the region.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's semi-annual assessment of countries it deems are outright manipulators or should be on watch-lists for such behaviour is due as soon as this week.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam, which was named a manipulator for the first time in Treasury's December report, appears to have continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and may stay on the list.\par \par \uc2 Thailand and Taiwan could also be named as manipulators this time. Others, including China, Japan, South Korea, Germany, Italy, Singapore, Malaysia and Hong Kong, are likely to join or remain on the Treasury's 'monitoring list' of countries that meet some of the criteria for being labelled as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators. "With most of the U.S. major trading partners in Asia either being labelled a manipulator or on the monitoring list, there is now less stigma associated with being called out by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 ," said Khoon Goh, head of Asia research at ANZ in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 A 2015 U.S. law which can lead to sanctions, bases the manipulator designation on three criteria - a $20 billion-plus trade surplus with the United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeding 2% of gross domestic product and a current account surplus exceeding 2% of GDP.\par \par \uc2 The label of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator does not automatically bring any punishment, however, and the U.S. law only requires Washington to demand negotiations with designated countries.\par \par \uc2 The April report will be the first since \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  was appointed by U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to lead the Treasury.\par \par \uc2 While not counting on it, analysts such as Goh wonder if the new administration will make allowances for the effects of the coronavirus pandemic, loose U.S. monetary policies and the U.S.-China trade war in distorting trade balances and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values in Asia.\par \par \uc2 "We doubt that the \uc2 U.S Treasury\uc2  will get far from their bilateral engagements unless there is recognition of the role that U.S. policies have played in the first place," ANZ's Goh said in a note.\par \par \uc2 LEVERAGE\par \par \uc2 The Treasury allows itself plenty of discretion. China, for instance, became the first country to be properly named a manipulator at the height of the trade war in 2019, even though it didn't meet all the three criteria.\par \par \uc2 This time, despite a massive current account surplus in 2020, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have barely risen. The yuan has steadied over the past six months, and rising dollar balances at local banks have analysts suspecting that they are massaging the flows in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stead.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland, a first-time manipulator in the December report, could escape that tag because it appears to have scaled-back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, although it might remain on the monitoring list.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam has benefited from a shift in exports and manufacturing of electronics and other goods from China after its trade war with Washington. Since December, when it was labelled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used special \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to keep its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  off the books for a while.\par \par \uc2 Nguyen Tri Hieu, a former Vietnam government advisor, believes authorities in the Southeast Asian country do worry about the possible damage to its reputation and exports from being named a manipulator.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think Biden administration would remove Vietnam from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator list in the short term. Instead, the U.S. will use it as leverage in further negotiations with Vietnam, but no sanctions or taxes will be levied," Hieu said.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers in Taiwan say they have observed that countries already tagged by the United States, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have not felt any impact.\par \par \uc2 "In fact, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in small and open economies is like other countries' quantitative easing - they are all important monetary policy tools for the central banks to achieve their legally defined missions," \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. (Additional reporting by Liang-Sa Loh in Taipei, Andrew Galbraith in Shanghai, Writing by Vidya Ranganathan, Editing by Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-4-13T11:53:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210413eh4d017o9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
