\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-U.S. trade chief voices concern to Vietnam over  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  practices\b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2021\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds Vietnam trade ministry comment, background)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, April 1 (Reuters) - U.S. Trade Representative Katherine Tai, in a call on Thursday with Vietnam's minister of industry and trade, highlighted U.S. concerns about Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices, a USTR statement said.\par \par \uc2 Tai and the Vietnamese minister \uc2 Tran Tuan Anh\uc2  also "discussed U.S. concerns on illegal timber practices, digital trade and agriculture," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's Ministry of Industry and Trade\uc2  in a statement on Friday said Vietnam and the United States "will continue to actively cooperate to comprehensively address the concerns to maintain a stable trade relation."\par \par \uc2 The ministry said bilateral trade between the two countries is expected to reach $100 billion this year, up from $90.8 billion last year. The United States is Vietnam's largest export market.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  in December labeled Vietnam a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator" due to its growing trade surplus with the United States, its large global current account surplus and heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the value of its dong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In January, the USTR released the results of an investigation into Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices.\par \par \uc2 It found Vietnam's actions to push down the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were "unreasonable" and restricted U.S. commerce, but it did not take immediate action to impose punitive tariffs.\par \par \uc2 In February, Reuters exclusively reported that \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, using what traders described as an unusual method. (Reporting by Eric Beech; Additional reporting by Khanh Vu; Editing by Leslie Adler and Grant McCool) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-4-2T04:46:57.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210401eh41040ix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
