\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  cuts down on dong  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  frequency\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2021\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * SBV says to buy USD weekly instead of daily\par \par \uc2 * SBV says aim is to let market set dong rates\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sensitive since U.S. branded VN a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator" (Adds backround, market price and further SBV comment)\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Phuong Nguyen\par \par \uc2 HANOI, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam (SBV) \uc2 said it has cut the frequency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the Vietnamese dong to move in accordance with the market.\par \par \uc2 "From Feb. 17, 2021, the SBV reduced the frequency of buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to once a week on every Wednesday, instead of daily," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in an email to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "This move aims at letting the rate move in accordance with the market."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a sensitive issue for \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the United States branded it a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator" in December for seeking to keep the dong from rising.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam has seen a surge in export-led growth and a higher value for the dong could hurt its manufacturers and threaten this growth in the middle of a pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Reuters earlier reported the SBV had this year ceased buying dollars in the spot market, where trades settle within days, and instead purchased them for delivery in July, a move traders said could help avoid drawing U.S. attention.\par \par \uc2 The SBV said it stopped spot transactions from Jan. 4 and instead shifted to using derivatives called forwards - including an unusual provision allowing banks to cancel them - in order to ensure a flexible rate for the dong and to support liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam has consistently said its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies aimed to maintain stability and control inflation, not seek trade advantage.\par \par \uc2 The dong has barely moved in official spot markets this year, with a 0.2% gain and quoted around 23,020 per dollar on Monday. (Reporting by \uc2 Phuong Nguyen\uc2  in Hanoi; Writing and additional reporting by Tom Westbrook in Singapore; Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Giles Elgood) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-2-22T16:16:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210222eh2m032q5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
