\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Vietnam banks should cut costs, interest rates -cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Add detail and background)\par \par \uc2 HANOI, March 31 (Reuters) - Vietnamese banks should consider cutting \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  costs, bonuses and cash dividends to focus on reducing interest rates amid the spread of the coronavirus, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam (SBV) \uc2 said controlling inflation and macroeconomic stability were top priorities.\par \par \uc2 "Banks should actively review and cut \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  expenses, especially salaries and bonuses, and promptly adjust business and financial plans to suit the current situation," it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Cash dividends should not be allocated this time to focus resources on reducing lending interest rates on current and new loans."\par \par \uc2 The SBV earlier cut key policy rates to prop up the economy and said it had enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resources to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy grew at its slowest pace in a decade in the first quarter, hit by the pandemic and the slow global economy, government data showed.\par \par \uc2 The Southeast Asian nation has 204 coronavirus infections, but reported no deaths, with more than 75,000 people in quarantine. (Reporting by Phuong Nguyen; Editing by Andrew Heavens and Nick Macfie) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-31T11:47:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200331eg3v0235l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\