\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam \highlight\uc2  c.bank willing to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  after dong hits record low\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2018\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HANOI, July 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ensure stability, its governor said on Monday after the dong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a record low last week.\par \par \uc2 The dong hit 22,965 to the dollar on Friday, a drop that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attributed to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise on global markets and recent falls on the Vietnamese stock market.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBV) \uc2 ... stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quoted governor Le Minh Hung as saying in a statement on its website.\par \par \uc2 "Currently we have all necessary tools and plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, ensuring the control of macroeconomic stability," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's foreign reserves have been hitting fresh record highs this year, standing at around $63.5 billion by end-June, up $11 billion from December last year, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign direct investment inflows rose 8.4 percent in the first half of 2018, while the Southeast Asian nation posted a trade surplus of $2.7 billion in the six-month period.\par \par \uc2 The stock market benchmark VN Index fell as low as 932.66 points on Monday, an intra-day level unseen in more than a month. The index has been retreating from a historic high hit in April of 1,211.34, Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 SBV said it will observe the market closely and is ready to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even at lower-than-market levels to ensure market and macroeconomic stability, the bank said in a separate statement on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The dong recovered slightly on Monday, trading at 22,952 to the dollar, Reuters data showed. (Reporting by Mai Nguyen; editing by David Stamp) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-2T15:27:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180702ee7200ir3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
