\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Vietnam scraps ceiling on individual dollar deposit rates after Fed move\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2015\par 17:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, rate moves, comments)\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Mai Nguyen\par \par \uc2 HANOI, Dec 17 (Reuters) - \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Thursday it was abolishing a ceiling for interest rates on dollar deposits that banks offer to individuals, in an attempt to "avoid dollar hoarding".\par \par \uc2 The move came hours after the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  raised interest rates for the first time in nearly a decade and less than three months after Vietnam cut the individual dollar deposit rate to 0.25 percent from 0.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The change will go into effect on Friday and was posted in a statement on the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2 's (SBV) website about an hour after it emailed comments to media, saying the bank will be "consistent with its interest rate and deposit measures".\par \par \uc2 "The rising \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate (in the domestic market) over the past days are due to psychological factors before the Fed's meeting to raise interest rates ... to 0.25 percent, and the falling yuan," Deputy Governor Nguyen Thi Hong said in the online comments.\par \par \uc2 "In terms of policy, SBV will stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," Hong said.\par \par \uc2 In August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  became one of the first countries in Asia to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after China devalued the yuan, by devaluing the dong by 1 percent and widening the dollar/dong band twice.\par \par \uc2 It had already devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice, each time by 1 percent, before to the yuan depreciation, even though Governor Nguyen Van Binh had promised to keep the dong within a 2 percent range, to Vietnam's export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2 The dong/dollar rate has been lingering near its ceiling since Tuesday as the U.S. rate increase came closer.\par \par \uc2 "Removing the individual dollar deposit rate is unlikely to help ease the dong/dollar rate, as proven with the scrapping of corporate rate earlier this year," said Do Quang Hop, deputy research manager of Saigon-Hanoi Securities.\par \par \uc2 "SBV will use all of its measures to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate stable, but the main issue here is that SBV anchors the rate to the U.S. dollar, which is hard to completely resolve," Hop said. (Reporting by \uc2 Mai Nguyen\uc2 , editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-12-17T17:14:33.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151217ebch00lzz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
