\par\par \b \uc2 Cross-Asset Class Moves Hint at Global Deleveraging -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2015\par 06:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0429 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Signs are appearing that a global deleveraging by investors may be underway. In recent days, bonds have sold off in the U.S. and the eurozone, sending yields significantly higher. Stocks have been sliding on mixed corporate earnings and a warning Wednesday from the U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  that valuations may be elevated. Most Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weakening Thursday, despite a second consecutive drop in the U.S. dollar index. Meanwhile, the euro has rallied to a three-month high despite lingering concerns of a Greek debt default, a sign that the consensus trade of being short EUR/USD due to contrasting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances is being unwound. If Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls report beats expectations, it could exacerbate deleveraging as investors brace for the U.S. Federal Reserve to end its near-zero interest rate policy. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0429 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to keep its benchmark interest rate unchanged when it meets this week, as lower commodity prices offset price pressures from a new consumption tax and economic growth likely remains within the bank's expectations. All 13 economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy committee to hold the overnight policy rate at 3.25% on Thursday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has kept the benchmark rate steady since July 2014. Malaysia's consumer price index rose 0.9% in March from a year earlier, while GDP expanded 5.8% from a year earlier in the fourth quarter, faster than the 5.6% growth in the third quarter. On April 30, Bank Negara Malaysia Governor Zeti Akhtar Aziz said the coming monetary policy review would consider mainly domestic factors, including the impact of the recently enforced goods and services tax, or the so-called called consumption tax, implemented on April 1. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0415 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Persistent supply shortage and modest rate hikes are reasons for Citi Research's bullish view on Hong Kong's property developers. With the market's overestimation of residential supply and continued rise in home prices, the house likes developers with "good launch pipelines in the city, attractive valuation and strong balance sheets". Top buys are Sun Hung Kai (0016.HK), Henderson Land (0012.HK), New World (0017.HK) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kerry Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0683.HK), it says. The house forecasts the city's home prices to rise 10% this year, from 8% previously, on top of a 16.5% rise since June 2014. It also expects modest hikes for the Fed fund rate, around 75bps a year, over the next three years. "A modest rate rise would help lift policy risk concerns and could be positive for developers' share prices," it adds. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @joannechiuhk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0413 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] At \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' (005930.SE) groundbreaking ceremony for the company's new $14.4 billion plant Thursday, South Korean President Park Geun-hye took several minutes to stress the need to boost the country's manufacturing power by moving to more cutting-edge technologies. Park, whose speech took much longer than that of Samsung chief executive Kwon Oh-hyun, took a moment to highlight the importance of investing in logic chips, a category of semiconductors that are used for processing computing orders such as the Exynos chips used in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Galaxy S6 smartphones. Unlike memory-chips, which have long been a profit-driver for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the company's logic-chip division has been described as a weak spot for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a laggard to rivals like \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Park's comments come amid an aggressive push by the Chinese government to foster its own chip power for economic and security reasons. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  hasn't disclosed whether the new Pyeongtaek plant, slated to start \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2017, will be used for making memory-chips or logic chips. (min-jeong.lee@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0411 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] ANZ Research says Vietnam's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may further devalue its dong later this year, following Thursday's 1% devaluation against the U.S. dollar. "We maintain that the VND could reach 22,050 by year-end, taking the annual depreciation spot to 3.1%, compared to the 1.4% decline in 2014," ANZ Research says in a note. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sets the dollar rate at 21,673 Vietnamese dong Thursday versus 21,458 dong Wednesday. "Today's devaluation will help to bring the trade account closer to balance, as against defending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," it says. Although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Vietnam\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign reserves have been on a rise (at $35 billion), reserves provide a relatively low import coverage of some 2.5 months, below the average recommended level of 3-4 months, it notes. It adds that even with today's devaluation, the dong still trades in line with other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0409 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The burgeoning alliance between Japan and the Philippines took a significant step forwards this week, as the two countries' Coast Guards conducted their first joint exercises since Manila and Tokyo signed a new strategic pact in 2012. Since then, the partners have moved ever closer together thanks to shared concerns about China's military rise, and also with Japanese manufacturers keen to expand in the Philippines to take advantage of the country's improving business environment, and escape rising costs elsewhere. Following this week's anti-piracy drills in Manila Bay, President Benigno Aquino is set to make a state visit to Japan next month to further solidify the relationship. The first of 10 new Philippine Coast Guard ships under construction in Japan courtesy of a $164 million loan provided by Tokyo are expected to arrive soon after to help boost the Philippines' ability to monitor its territorial waters--and keep tabs on Chinese activities offshore. (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0404 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD is higher on increasing foreign fund outflows, says a local trader. "The Korean won has fallen much this morning, so the Taiwan dollar just followed," the trader says, adding that exporter sales [of USD] still capped the greenback's gains at around 30.700. The USD/TWD is at 30.688, higher than 30.600 traded before the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday, which lifted it to 30.753 at the close of onshore trading session, traders say. Taiwan government bonds consolidate on thin volume ahead of the U.S. non-farm payroll report Friday; the most-traded five-year bond yield is at 1.0590% versus 1.0525% late Wednesday. Taiwan shares are down 0.8%. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0357 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY, now at 119.50, could break above 121 if U.S. jobs data out Friday prove surprisingly strong, says Kyosuke Suzuki, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and money market sales at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The possibility of reaching the Y121 mark can't be ruled out," if impressive numbers comfortably exceed the market consensus of 230,000 new jobs created in April. Since the pair already hit 120.51 on May 5, there may now be less resistance capping the upside below 121. Favorable initial unemployment claims later tonight could lay the groundwork for movement toward the upside, making a challenge on Y121 more realistic, he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0353 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Australia's Liberal-National coalition government is likely to reintroduce the idea of a "co-payment," where patients pay a fee to see a general practitioner. But this time there'll be some "subtle massaging" of any policy proposal to make it more palatable to voters, Robert Cooke, chief executive of Healthscope (HSO.AU), tells a conference. "I think it's inevitable that a co-payment in some shape or form emerges across a range of things, whether it's pharmacy or the GP," he says. "It won't be across the board and badly announced, badly implemented." The government recently scrapped a proposed A$7 across-the-board fee after voters and medical practitioners balked at the idea. (ross.kelly@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are broadly softer against the U.S. dollar alongside a sell-off in regional stocks and bonds. The Korean won is the biggest mover, falling 0.7% against the greenback, followed by the Malaysian ringgit, which dropped 0.5%. "There's risk-off move in the markets," said Paul Mackel, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's head of global emerging markets \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research. There's been some spillover impact from the volatility in bond market into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, including Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Also, there's an unwinding of euro-funded carry trades amid a stronger euro "that's been squeezing out other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ", he said. In China, the yuan is relatively resilient amid the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's effort to stabilize its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the fixing for the yuan at 6.1113 per dollar--the strongest level since February last year. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] OCBC says the announcement by \f28 \uc2 \f2 M1 Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (B2F.SG) that it has signed an agreement to buy a 15% equity stake in Integrated Telecommunications Oman for about US$7.8 million is a positive for Singapore's smallest telecommunications services provider. OCBC keeps unchanged its 'Hold' recommendation for M1 and fair value estimate of S$3.66 for now. "While it is still early days, we believe the news is positive as the move could signal a significant change in the telco's Singapore-only strategy," OCBC says. M1 gains 1.4% to S$3.57, while the benchmark FTSE Straits Times Index is down 0.5%. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7 May 2015 00:29 ET \par Cross-Asset Class Moves Hint at Global -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0328 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 M1 Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (B2F.SG) gains 1.4% to S$3.57 after Singapore's smallest telecommunications services provider announces that it has signed an agreement to buy a 15% equity stake in Integrated Telecommunications Oman for about US$7.8 million. M1's investment in Oman's first private international gateway operator and mobile services reseller will help the Singapore-listed firm expand. Analysts have often criticized M1 for being primarily focused on the small, highly competitive market of Singapore. The possibility of a fourth mobile operator in Singapore would hurt M1 the most, analysts say. With the government likely to auction more bandwidth this year, two firms have already shown interest in bidding for a telecom license. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 07, 2015 00:29 ET (04:29 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150507eb57000f5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
