\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  to Stabilize USD/VND Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nguyen Pham Muoi   \par \uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2013\par 04:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HANOI--The \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stabilize the dollar/dong rate, including selling the U.S. dollar in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dong rate has become volatile in recent days after the dong was weakened by a 1% devaluation on June 26.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fixed the USD/VND rate at 21,036 Thursday, but \uc2 Vietcombank\uc2  is quoting at 21,230-21,246, unchanged from Wednesday, and the goldshops in Hanoi quote at 21,550-21,600, down from 21,600-21,650 a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 "The USD/VND exchange rate has become volatile recently not because of the demand and supply imbalance but because some local banks have bought (the dollar) as they have a surplus of dong funds," Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Le Minh Hung said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not ruled out that some speculators are involved in illegal trade of the dollar," Mr. Hung noted.\par \par \uc2 Due to its rising \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves so far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take necessary measures to stabilize the dong, including adjusting the interest rates, curbing inflation and preventing illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading activities in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he added.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam is capable of keeping the dong stable because the country only had a trade deficit of $1.4 billion in the first half of the year, equivalent to 2.3% of its total export values, Mr. Hung said.\par \par \uc2 The economy's earnings of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is high after the disbursement of foreign direct investment hit $5.7 billion in the first half, while the inflows of indirect investment by foreigners and remittance from Vietnamese overseas have also risen, he said.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's current account is expected to have a total surplus of $5 billion this year, Mr. Hung added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nguyen Pham Muoi at phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com [ 11-07-13 0251GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130711e97b0001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
