\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support dong -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 By John Ruwitch   \par \uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2011\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HANOI, Sept 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling U.S. dollars to banks in recent weeks to support the weak dong , which has come under pressure since early August following months of stability, market sources said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  (SBV) has sold an estimated $1.5 billion to five or six large state-run and partly-private banks since mid-August, two sources who closely follow the Vietnamese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market estimated.\par \par \uc2 Two other sources declined to estimate the total value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said some banks had been sold between $15 million and $35 million a day over about three weeks.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is not unprecedented for the SBV, but past attempts have proven ineffective at sustainably supporting the dong, which has fallen by more than 20 percent against the dollar since mid-2008.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Nguyen Van Binh declined to comment when asked about the dollar sales late last week. Other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have also declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The sliding dong has been one of a host of problems plaguing Vietnam's once-promising economy, along with spiraling inflation, a debilitating trade deficit, lumbering state enterprises and slow responses to power shortages and other infrastructure woes.\par \par \uc2 In February, the SBV devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 8.5 percent, the biggest devaluation since the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis, and pledged flexibility on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The government also instituted a series of measures to try to de-dollarise the economy. This helped stabilise the dong for a time, during which the SBV compelled state-owned enterprises to sell it their dollars from exports.\par \par \uc2 The government said last week the bank had purchased $6 billion since the start of 2011 to beef up its dwindling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  war chest.\par \par \uc2 The volume of dollars the SBV has sold in its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the dong has been "significant in terms of total reserve size," said one source.\par \par \uc2 The SBV does not divulge the current level of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but a senior government advisor told Reuters last month the total had slipped to $7 billion to $8 billion earlier this year. It was $23 billion in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has been more flexible on setting\par \par \uc2 the dong's midpoint . From April 19 to July 9, the midpoint strengthened 125 dong to 20,608 dong and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded mostly within its band of 1 percent on either side of that rate.\par \par \uc2 But success in stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hurt in early August when a rise in global gold prices sparked renewed pressure. The unofficial rate resumed trading outside the official band, traders say.\par \par \uc2 Since Aug. 24, the midpoint has been unchanged at 20,628 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Aug. 11, Binh was quoted in an interview with a state-run newspaper as saying the State Bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "when there are problems with demand and supply."\par \par \uc2 He added: "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at this moment allow us to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the necessary level."\par \par \uc2 Bouts with double-digit inflation as well as wide trade and budget deficits have hurt the dong, which locals nimbly dump whenever uncertainty arises or gold prices surge.\par \par \uc2 For a daily look at dong exchange rates, click\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jason Szep and Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 VIETNAM-ECONOMY/DOLLARS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110906e7960006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
