\par\par \b \uc2 Vietnam Money-Rates stabilise, but maybe not for long -bankers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ngo Thi Ngoc Chau   \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2010\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HANOI, Dec 20 (Reuters) - Deposit and interbank rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  have fallen over the past week after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities but bankers said there were signs this might not last very long.\par \par \uc2  Most lenders brought deposit rates down to 14 percent after the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  imposed this as the ceiling rate on Dec. 15 and threatened to punish those that ignored the cap. [ID:nHAN214216]\par \par \uc2  Dong interbank rates also eased, with the overnight rate down at 10.14 percent on Monday, the lowest in two weeks, Reuters data showed. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  For the latest interest rate fixings, click        <VNIBOS>\par  For details on open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           <SBVOMO2010>\par  For the latest SBV banking review, click    [ID:nSGE6B808F]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  However, state media reported on Monday that some banks\par were trying to circumvent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's regulation by\par giving depositors bonuses or signing "investment cooperation"\par contracts with them, which pushed the actual rates up to 15-16\par percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Several banks still need liquidity and some businesses are\par eager to get loans even at high rates despite lower profits,\par the Vietnam Economic Times quoted a bank executive as saying.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In the interbank market, banks had almost exclusively\par tapped overnight loans over the past week to manage short-term\par liquidity, said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader who declined to be named.\par There was very little trading in longer terms and rates were\par stable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The fact that there were only short-term transactions may\par be a sign that the stability of the market could be\par vulnerable," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Bankers said there was a difference in liquidity conditions\par between large and small banks, with the smaller ones trying to\par raise deposits while some larger players had extra cash.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Unusually, not all of the cash on offer from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week in open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was taken up because\par large institutions that have access to it were flush, while\par smaller banks in need of money were not eligible for the loans,\par the manager of a large bank in Hanoi said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Large banks have ample funds," she said. Several lenders\par were restricting their interbank loans to short terms and\par cutting longer-term lending in a defensive move at the end of\par the year, she added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Smaller banks cannot access \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loans via open\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because they generally do not hold treasury\par notes to offer as collateral.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  MARKET SUMMARY -                      Dec 20  Dec 13 Change\par                                                       (pct)\par  VND onshore interbank quotes <VND=VN>    19,495  19,495  \par 0.00\par  VND unofficial <VNDUNOFF=>               21,120  21,070 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -0.24\par  Ho Chi Minh Stock Exchange index <.VNI>  478.29  490.22 \par -2.43\par  Hanoi Stock Exchange index <.HNXI>       116.70  121.76  -4.16\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (VND quotes in the summary are bid rates).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  NEWS HIGHLIGHTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - Vietnam revised up its trade deficit for the first 11\par months of this year to $10.97 billion from an earlier estimate\par of $10.66 billion. [ID:nSGE6BJ020]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - Moody's Investors Service lowered Vietnam's sovereign\par rating on Wednesday, citing the heightened risk of a balance of\par payments crisis, accelerating inflation, a falling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par debt distress from state shipbuilder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vinashin\f28 \uc2 \f2 . [ID:nSGE6BE06O]\par  (Editing by John Ruwitch and Alan Raybould)\par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-VIETNAM/RATES|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101220e6ck000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
