\par\par \b \uc2 Reuters Southeast Asia News Highlights 0900 GMT Dec 3\b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its benchmark overnight rate at a record low of 6.50 percent, as expected, and said that the current rate level was in line with its 2010 inflation target. [ID:nJAK205233]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - Brokers may cut profit forecasts for Thailand's top two companies, PTT and \uc2 Siam Cement\uc2 , because a court ruling on environmental concerns could delay the start of new \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a huge industrial estate.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Administrative Court halted most new projects at the Map Ta Phut estate, home to the world's eighth-biggest petrochemicals hub, on Wednesday, rattling investors in Thailand and posing a new challenge for the government. [ID:nBKK477201]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast policy rates to remain on hold at a record low throughout 2010, but investors were convinced that a rise was likely in the first half of next year given an expected pickup in inflation.\par \par \uc2 Senior deputy governor and currently acting governor Darmin Nasution had said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may leave rates where they are in 2010 given inflation is forecast to be within of its target of 4-6 percent next year, in sharp contrast to market expectations for a rise as early as first quarter next year. [ID:nJAK405023]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 HANOI - \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a "very big scale" to stabilise the beleaguered dong, backed by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of more than $16 billion, a deputy governor said.\par \par \uc2 The comments by Nguyen Van Binh come a week after Vietnam devalued the dong for the third time since the start of 2008 to relieve pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of dollar hoarding. [ID:nSP96429]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE - Singapore, a Southeast Asian city-state with high per-capita emissions, will head to global climate talks next week with a pledge to cut carbon pollution by 16 percent versus projected business-as-usual levels by 2020.\par \par \uc2 This "stretch target" is based on the level of greenhouse gas emissions that Singapore would produce by 2020 if no proactive measures to cut them were taken, but relies on a legal deal being reached after the U.N. talks in Copenhagen, ministers said. [ID:nSP257502]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 HANOI - It is "reassuring" to see Vietnam rebalancing its economic policy toward stability, but more turbulence could be in the cards as the global economy continues to recover, the World Bank said.\par \par \uc2 Even as Vietnam tightens monetary policy, inflation is likely to see some acceleration in 2010, it said in a semi-annual report. [ID:nSP69338]\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Carl Bagh)\par \par \uc2 ((Bangalore Editorial Reference Unit;+91 80 41355917;RM carl.bagh@thomsonreuters.com))\par \par \uc2 SOUTHEAST ASIA-HIGHLIGHTS 0900 GMT|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|G|SI|PHD|IF|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091203e5c3000is\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
