\par\par \b \uc2 Vietnam orders oil, coal producers to sell  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -report\b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 05:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HANOI, Nov 27 (Reuters) - The Vietnamese government has ordered the country's two biggest exporters, state oil monopoly \uc2 Petrovietnam\uc2  and coal monopoly Vinacomin, to sell their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help bridge a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shortfall.\par \par \uc2 The daily Tuoi Tre quoted a directive by Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung as ordering the two groups to "immediately sell whenever they have \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income" to the \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  "so that the bank can have foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market".\par \par \uc2 The government has also asked a number of other unidentified state-run companies to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the report said.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how much foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vinacomin and \uc2 Petrovietnam\uc2  own but statistics showed combined crude oil exports and coal exports in the first 11 months of $6.94 billion. (Reporting by Nguyen Nhat Lam; Editing by Jan Dahinten) ((nhatlam.nguyen@thomsonreuters.com; +844 3825 9623; Reuters Messaging: nhatlam.nguyen.reuters.com@thomsonreuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com))\par \par \uc2 VIETNAM-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|SI|RNP|DNP|PEN   