\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - Vietnam newspapers - Nov 26\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 02:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HANOI, Nov 26 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in the official Vietnamese press on Thursday. Reuters has not verified these stories.\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL NEWS:\par \par \uc2 TUOI TRE\par \par \uc2 -- The State Securities Commission has put in place new regulations to curb short selling of stocks, and they will go into effect on Dec. 1.\par \par \uc2 -- Many small companies started selling dollars after the \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, bankers said.\par \par \uc2 THANH NIEN\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  Property Fund Ltd\uc2  will raise its stake in Hoang Anh Gia Lai to 0.25 percent by Jan. 15, 2010.\par \par \uc2 THOI BAO KINH TE VIET NAM\par \par \uc2 -- Oricombank will raise 2 trillion dong ($108.2 million) via short-term bills from Nov. 26 to Dec. 31.\par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC AND GENERAL NEWS:\par \par \uc2 HANOI MOI\par \par \uc2 -- The death toll from the H1N1 flu virus outbreak has risen to 43, health officials said.\par \par \uc2 -- The lifting of the gold import ban has not helped bridge the gap between local and international gold prices with local prices still about 3 million dong per tael higher than world prices, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 SAIGON GIAI PHONG\par \par \uc2 -- Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung praised diplomats at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for their efforts in border negotiations with China.\par \par \uc2 THANH NIEN\par \par \uc2 -- State Bank Governor Nguyen Van Giau said Vietnamese businesses hold about $10.3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts at banks. Giau said some major state-run exporters would have to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of efforts to raise dollar funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 -- The National Assembly has approved a plan to build two nuclear power plants at a cost of 200 trillion dong, or nearly $11 billion. (Reporting by Hanoi Newsroom) ((hanoi.newsroom@reuters.com; +844 3825 9623)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com))\par \par \uc2 VIETNAM-PRESS|LANGEN|G|RBN|SI|REVU|RNP|DNP|PGE|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091126e5bq0002d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
