\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Vietnam devalues dong, but some see further decline\b0\par\par\uc2 1,065 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2009\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * New band is +/-3 pct compared with +/-5 pct previously\par \par \uc2 * Key policy rates increased by 1 percentage point\par \par \uc2 * Governor says weighed pros and cons\par \par \uc2 * Solution now "is to strongly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", Giau says\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say dong weakness could continue\par \par \uc2 (Adds IMF reaction, paragraph 8)\par \par \uc2 By John Ruwitch and Nguyen Nhat Lam\par \par \uc2 HANOI, Nov 25 (Reuters) - Vietnam scrambled on Wednesday to relieve pressure on the beleaguered dong in the face of dollar hoarding, devaluing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raising interest rates and saying it will call on some exporters to sell their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While devaluing the dong more than 5 percent, the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  also said it would narrow the dong's trading band against the dollar to 3 percent either side of a daily mid point set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Previous attempts to control a long-term slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  included two devaluations last year and widening the dong's trading band several times, but they had little effect and left it facing persistent selling pressure for more than a year.\par \par \uc2 "This time our solution is to strongly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Nguyen Van Giau said on Wednesday, after officials had repeatedly said the dong would not be devalued.\par \par \uc2 Stocks fell sharply on Wednesday after the news. The new dong rate becomes effective on Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Dollar hoarding is widespread in Vietnam among ordinary people and companies alike. Many big-ticket business transactions are done in dollars, but dollar supplies have been squeezed by the global financial crisis, which hit big \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earners such as exports, remittances and foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 Previous devaluations have helped feed expectations for yet further devaluations. Exporters have held on to their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in expectation of an announcement like Wednesday's, despite protestations from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The IMF's senior representative in Vietnam said the steps were bolder than many had expected and sent a positive signal about the government's intent to tackle macroeconomic risks. "We are encouraged," said Benedict Bingham.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts doubted the moves would prevent further pressure on the dong from emerging, partly because the country is running external deficits.\par \par \uc2 The dong is probably still overvalued and the credibility of Vietnam's policymakers is at risk, said Standard Chartered Bank economist Tai Hui.\par \par \uc2 "Given the trade deficit and the current account deficit, I would suspect the dong remains overvalued," he said. "We will continue to see expectations of more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation. But the latest move will help relieve some of the pressure for now."\par \par \uc2 CONTRASTING FORTUNES\par \par \uc2 The dong's fortunes in 2009 are in stark contrast to those of most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are rising strongly in reaction to a flood of foreign investment. Indeed, both Brazil and Taiwan have impose capital controls to limit the inflows.\par \par \uc2 The dong though had fallen almost 12 percent on unofficial markets from the start of the year up to Wednesday, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had allowed the official mid-point to fall only 0.35 percent. After the news, the dong rose to around 19,450 in Hanoi on unofficial markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rationed dollars in the banking system to combat the tightness of supplies.\par \par \uc2 A treasurer at a foreign bank in Vietnam said he expected unofficial and interbank exchange rates to converge in coming weeks but that problems would persist, in part because the state bank lacked sufficient reserves for sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reserves fell to $16.5 billion in August from $23 billion at the end of 2008, World Bank figures show. At the end of September, only Pakistan and Bangladesh in Asia had smaller reserves among the economies monitored regularly by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Giau told reporters the benchmark base interest rate would be lifted to 8 percent from 7 percent on Dec. 1. Other key rates will also rise 1 percentage point, to bolster the dong and to fight inflation. [ID:nHAN481106]\par \par \uc2 Double digit inflation remains a raw memory in Vietnam, another reason why many Vietnamese hold dollars. On Wednesday, the government's statistics office estimated November's annual inflation was 4.35 percent. The 2009 cumulative trade gap up to October was $8.78 billion. November data is due this week.\par \par \uc2 To get more dollars flowing in the economy, the prime minister would request some major exporters to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Giau said without giving details.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's stock markets fell on the news. The Ho Chi Minh Stock Index shed 4.5 percent and the Hanoi index lost almost 6 percent on concern the moves would slow down the economy.\par \par \uc2 CALCULATED PROS AND CONS\par \par \uc2 "We have calculated all the pros and cons of the adjustment," Giau said. "Our national debt obligation will increase. The move will also have an impact on companies borrowing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 But there would be benefits, he added, including improved exports and increased tax revenue from importers, while higher interest rates would help cap credit growth, which rose 34.5 percent between January and November.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sbv.gov.vn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.sbv.gov.vn}}}\uc2 ) said the new mid-point rate of 17,961 dong would take effect on Thursday. On Wednesday, the rate was 17,034, more than 5 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities know that there is a lot of market pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate, and they want to accommodate some of that, but they don't want to accommodate too much that would make people feel the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in a free fall," said Tim Condon, head of Asia research at ING in Singapore. LINKS > Analysts' comments............. [ID:nSP525641] > Fitch Ratings' view of the moves............... [ID:nT354852] > Timeline on Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy changes.. [ID:nSP78611] > Timeline on Vietnam's interest rate changes...[ID:nHAN137641] > November inflation report..... [ID:nHAN481106] (Additional reporting by Kevin Yao in SINGAPORE and Umesh Desai in HONG KONG; Editing by Jason Szep and Neil Fullick) ((john.ruwitch@thomsonreuters.com; +84 4 3825 9623; Reuters Messaging: john.ruwitch.reuters.com@reuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com))\par \par \uc2 VIETNAM-\b \highlight22\uc2 