\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 2-Vietnam to allow gold imports to stabilise market\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2009\par 02:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats from Wednesday without changes)\par \par \uc2  * Vietnam relaxes gold ban in place since May '08\par \par \uc2  * No volume limit, but only 5 or 6 firms can import  (Updates with details)\par \par \uc2  By John Ruwitch and Ho Binh Minh\par \par \uc2  HANOI, Nov 11 (Reuters) - Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday lifted a 1-1/2-year-old ban on gold imports in a bid to stabilise the market after a sharp rise in prices helped drive the country's dong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record low.\par \par \uc2  "The \uc2 State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow gold imports with a volume sufficient to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in order to stabilise the market, combat speculation and prevent an impact on the interests of the people," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its Web site, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sbv.gov.vn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.sbv.gov.vn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Five or six companies would be allowed to import unlimited quantities of gold, state-run news Web site VNexpress.net quoted \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  Governor Nguyen Van Giau as saying on Wednesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2  He did not give details or a timeframe.\par \par \uc2  The ban on gold imports since May 2008 led to a gap between domestic and international prices, and recently traders say that spread, plus the rise in gold prices globally, triggered a surge in demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2  "This morning the prices and the market went crazy, the worst time in my 20 years of trading," an owner of a gold shop in Hanoi's downtown district of Hoan Kiem said.\par \par \uc2  "Prices collapsed this afternoon and the decision on gold imports will certainly help control the situation."\par \par \uc2  By early afternoon on Wednesday the dong hit 19,800 per dollar -- about 7 percent lower than the rate a week ago -- before rebounding to around 19,000.\par \par \uc2  For a Q+A on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , click: [ID:nHAN491590]\par \par \uc2  Gold leapt above 29 million dong per tael on Wednesday, or $1,261 per troy ounce at an exchange rate of 19,000 dong per dollar. Later it deflated to around 27.5 million dong. Last Wednesday it was at about 24.5 million dong per tael.\par \par \uc2  Internationally, gold <XAU=> has gained more than 25 percent in 2009, driven by persistent weakness in the U.S. dollar, expectations of more buying from central banks and fears about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2  It shot to a record high at $1,117.05 an ounce on Wednesday as the dollar slipped to its lowest in more than a year, lifting bullion's appeal as an alternative investment.\par \par \uc2  TURNING AWAY CUSTOMERS\par \par \uc2  The government responded to the price spikes earlier in the day by dispatching inspectors to gold shops, which double as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  changers, dealers said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules allow the dong to trade with the dollar within a band of 5 percent on either side of a reference rate it sets each day. A rate of 19,800 dong per dollar is more than triple the limit.\par \par \uc2  By early afternoon, gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes were brought back down but some shops were turning away walk-in customers. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  blamed domestic speculators for pushing the gold price above world levels.\par \par \uc2  Offshore dealers covering Vietnam said gold bars had been smuggled in from neighbouring countries to meet growing demand.\par \par \uc2  "The thing is, people are cautious," a dealer in Singapore said. "The domestic price is so high because they haven't imported gold for a long time. Basically, there's a shortage of physical gold."\par \par \uc2  Vietnam consumed 115.8 tonnes of gold for jewellery and investment in 2008, up from 77.5 tonnes in 2007.\par \par \uc2  Traditionally, the Vietnamese use gold for savings, jewellery and real estate transactions but when inflation is high, many choose gold or the U.S. dollar to hedge against inflation.  (Additional reporting by Lewa Pardomuan in Singapore; Editing by Clarence Fernandez)    \par \par \uc2 VIETNAM-GOLD/ (UPDATE 2, PIX, REPEAT)|LANGEN|SI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091112e5bc0002f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
