\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam \highlight\uc2  Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Stabilize Dong - Report \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1997\par 09:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HANOI, \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected millions of U.S. dollars into money markets in an effort to stabilize the dong after it's continued drop in black market trading, official media reported Monday. \par \par \uc2  The bank's deputy governor, Le Duc Thuy, told reporters the Vietnamese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would level off at about 12,300 dong against the dollar, the official Saigon Times Daily reported. \par \par \uc2  The State Bank of Vietnam earlier this month effectively devalued the dong, by expanding the trading band within which it can fluctuate against the dollar and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Within days of the move, the dong had dropped from about 11,600 per dollar to 13,200 at some black market trading houses. \par \par \uc2  The devaluation was prompted by Southeast Asia's regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. Vietnam's artificially inflated dong was driving export prices up compared with neighboring competitors. \par \par \uc2  Although the expanded plus or minus 10% trading band officially allows the dong to drop to about 12,300 against the dollar, black market trading drove the price even lower. \par \par \uc2  'The change was essentially of a psychological nature,' Thuy was quoted as telling the state-run Vietnam News Agency. \par \par \uc2  Thuy said Vietnam's reserves were plentiful enough to limit the fallout on the dong and stabilize both dollar and gold prices. \par \par \uc2  In the first 10 days after the dong's trading band was expanded, the state bank sold about $75 million to various commercial banks, the newspaper reported. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0845GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtar0834n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
