\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk/Trading Band -2:Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If Necessary \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 1997\par 11:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HO CHI MINH CITY, \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the State Bank of Vietnam, has no plans to widen the dong's trading band again, or dramatically adjust the central rate set daily by the bank governor's office, a State Bank official told Dow Jones Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The official, who declined to be named, said, 'We have no plans in the coming times to adjust the target rate.' \par \par \uc2  His comments followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move Monday to widen the trading band to plus or minus 10% from the central rate, which widened the band from the previous band of plus or minus 5% that had been in place since March. \par \par \uc2  The official said the move was to 'help the buyer and seller to meet each other.' \par \par \uc2  The State Bank's move Monday contradicted repeated bank statements that it would not widen the band. \par \par \uc2  Bankers and economists had called for a weaker dong in light of the current spate of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations. Vietnamese officials had said they were worried about Vietnam's export competitiveness, given the competition from the country's Asian neighbors. \par \par \uc2  Vietnam's trade deficit was $4.0 billion in 1996, and the government hopes to narrow it to $3.3 billion in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The official, who works in State Bank of Vietnam Deputy Governor Le Duc Thuy's office, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dong if it is necessary for the economy. \par \par \uc2  'We will support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the exchange rate and benefit the economy,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The official declined to confirm media reports that Vietnam's foreign reserves stand at $2.5 billion, or enough to cover 10 weeks of imports. \par \par \uc2  In Vietnam, such information is a 'state secret,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, the State Bank set the target rate for the dong at 11,171 dong to the dollar, up from Tuesday's 11,176 dong to the dollar. After the bank was widened, the dong fell to the floor of the band, and has remained there ever since. \par \par \uc2  At late afternoon, the dollar stood at 12,250 dong in very thin trade. Bankers said traders aren't willing to sell dollars at these levels because they're hoping for a further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0927GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtaf07p2x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
