\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Thai package leaves SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  cold. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1997\par 13:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 14 (Reuters) - Thailand's eagerly awaited financial reform package provoked scarcely a sound in Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Tuesday as traders found little cause for celebration. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht drifted slightly lower in offshore markets after easing on afternoon rumours that Thailand would lift its two-tier exchange rate system as part of the reform package. \par \par \uc2  "It's the same old crap we've seen for so long. That's probably why the dollar/baht is a bit higher now because most of the offshore players are disappointed," said a senior regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the baht's downside would be limited to 36.80 in offshore markets. It was at 36.10/40 to the dollar offshore at 1030 GMT against 35.90/36.00 six hours earlier. The onshore rate was little changed at 36.45/55. \par \par \uc2  Thai officials announced measures, including legislation to create two agencies to restructure and manage suspended Thai finance firms, requirements for financial institutions to raise their capital and amendments to bankruptcy laws. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi said Thailand had no plans to close any more financial institutions in addition to the 58 finance firms already suspended. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Thailand relaxed conditions for the 58 finance firms to resume business, increasing the time allowed them to repay a combined 430 billion baht borrowed from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from three years to eight. \par \par \uc2  "From the looks of it, there's nothing new. The reaction came before the release of the package on the rumours about the two-tier market," said Ishak Ismail, market intelligence analyst at I.D.E.A. \par \par \uc2  Other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained within earlier ranges, trading mainly on domestic factors. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar hit a low of 1.5440 to the U.S. dollar after Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong said the country would not emerge unhurt from the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  It recovered to 1.5384/94 to the U.S. dollar, near its opening levels but off an early high of around 1.5300. \par \par \uc2  "The reaction was a bit overdone because interbank and short-term players were just focusing on the one-liner, but his whole talk dealt with globalisation of markets," said Ishaq. \par \par \uc2  He said U.S. fund buying of the Malaysian ringgit against the Singapore dollar, in a reversal of earlier positions, had contributed to the Singapore dollar's drop. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit remained relatively firm at 3.1060/1110 to the U.S. dollar from an opening around 3.14 on local corporate demand ahead of the Malaysian budget on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was speculation Malaysian state oil firm Petronas may be behind some of the ringgit purchases through a large Malaysian bank. A Petronas spokesman declined comment. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was expected to keep to a 3.08-3.20 range before the budget. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was sandwiched between domestic corporate demand for dollars below the 3,450 rupiah level and talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 3,500. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared around 3,490 and sold a token amount of dollars, probably less than $50 million," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was at 3,470/3,500 to the dollar against an opening 3,450/3,500. Dealers said the market would be cautious before more details of the International Monetary Fund's aid programme for Indonesia became available. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended down at 34.13 to the dollar after thrice breaching its volatility band, causing it to be confined to a 31.514-34.139 band for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the peso's weakness was sparked by companies buying dollars to cover \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also failed to put up a strong defence after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the day. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Vietnam\b0 \highlight\uc2 's non-convertible dong became the latest victim of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rout as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the permitted trading band to 10 percent either side of the official daily rate from five percent, allowing it room to slide. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtae04a46\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Vietnam near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt